<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mário Soares</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1924–2017</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mário Soares was a Portuguese politician who founded the Socialist Party in exile in 1973 and helped steer Portugal to democracy after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carnation-revolution">Carnation Revolution</a> of 1974. He was prime minister from 1976 to 1978 and from 1983 to 1985, when he negotiated Portugal's entry into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-communities">European Community</a>, and president from 1986 to 1996.</p></div>
